{"id": "EUVD-2026-58999", "enisaUuid": "bd4101c9-f780-3117-a4fa-2e16123ebb97", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nespintcp: use sk_msg_free_partial to fix partial send\n\nsk_msg_free_partial() ensures consistency of the skmsg at every\niteration, without having to manually handle uncharges and offsets.\nThis simplifies the code, and fixes some bugs in skmsg accounting when\nwe don't send the full contents.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:52:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T21:19:24", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/518dcb84b997dff461800b079e5f2596389f766a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4ea8c051b4bd7feec7749a980f2f70e1782b84d7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a977f78adce40b39d90d9567e7987bb110102810", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/54d73f18f8919735f4d04d6f43374f75756c0180", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/14c0b42c8a2cd9b5361bbff45b52f69c62c6a286", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a66d45e0ce6d73cd79962d422388e61bfaf0cb50", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a338ce41bc933d8f74c39d9b3b6f1d8ca53d9714", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/007800408002d871f5699bdb944f985896730b8f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-55rh-f38r-fhcc", "CVE-2026-72041"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.76, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1d5459d0-dcaa-39f2-9c74-f2b4cd306d14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "1ec910df-aca5-34dc-87d7-0d303e840f92", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e27cca96cd68fa2c6814c90f9a1cfd36bb68c593 <a977f78adce40b39d90d9567e7987bb110102810"}, {"id": "2c30c6d3-5639-3fda-b84c-5787ef63bed0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.6"}, {"id": "32baede5-1b40-3f3d-abeb-12b44913cf79", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "p